    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-26144",
      "problem": "Consider the picture below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/d4f18c3567d0c55d3d6e002fbe2c6ac50b97b7adc14b016c8e95006de98ca15d.png)\n\nGiven that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/e10bd5483ec7194788a288e2fda950120c30a84f2e08887cf2c9dd859ad278b4.svg) find ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/44db815dcaf0a9d405026460a655495e055df7e55a785f542f8920ca90af5418.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "To find ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/4a2f3891f0b4c8b852767d556e1607028035219b70ab83b4910e95159a930b9c.svg) we want to match the expression\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/85cdb04eddb6da29d0abe34b048fe276fc8f5406ed481535447dde0ae9f99956.svg)\n\nWe are given that one of the components is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/72e7d33107ae13daba6b37f078b3d541891d9165c373cf4662b4de4e0d523ae4.svg) So, we first draw the vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/2b5d886d0eaf5c962aa46ccfe1d3b0caf6a471be4c5dd6067dcbc91968a3d038.svg) from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/278f99df1e14fe0ebfb61bdb72262a62670dcaa60d322148bc3ee591b278ec2d.svg)\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/65a6b5743ab9b6ef820744d0d6601b7dfd8de08a3f895661d96d2fe2cab8e0a7.png)\n\nLet ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/1aaddf0d4be4d873ff6c0600b0b239e0565a05ca8daaff7ca92bd5c70bebcf03.svg) be the endpoint of the vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/72e7d33107ae13daba6b37f078b3d541891d9165c373cf4662b4de4e0d523ae4.svg) Then\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/3a9a2959c3a256cb2651e0f00b0d7fe774f95aeee92289284bffb4c3b11b843a.svg)\n\nIn ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/9cad043ee64e1661ddddbcc39877a743638e49e35da1ddcb79da0d009cc29625.svg) we have:\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/d36dcb797fdd3eb9eb4df04f88695b86bcd480ee4beba23eaa2a04c5d1f49739.svg)\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/8fad9a79b79859bbfa05c67e2f567121e010601500ae3b53d1efc18c27ff1aed.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/639196a1a30d6f6280e3cf491e6cf3c2b0b991892970f7b641a9b300defb034f.svg) have opposite directions\n\nHence,\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/e9cc4740b7f188c4d1f0e65cf11721a8ea249e6ec623336782d08a9ca67fc057.svg)\n\nSimilarly,\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/b85266d772481528760f98b8fae0901d6505b679df8cc2c67aa1d39a5d4c7a3c.svg)\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/5f1f2cecb3a462fc45e60ec717c2fde5b1aaba79448a58aae1a9d3023b21b7bb.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/527e0abeb684dd24d8c92e45425542080c4c9493b9460bb89753fef3226c1f92.svg) have opposite directions\n\nHence,\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/b59a5af4e16f652c8a46443a16dca29b327d6bdec7a357e441dab25d781eea2e.svg)\n\nAdditionally,\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/8c23c72295a8afdb7b86369832e5b7fb79cdc67b165fa3b6e37f23a78ed394a6.svg)\n\nConsequently,\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/095805521b65ff1372bef215e634165e5ca0dcc7f188d62b00c7d795e89192a3.svg)\n\nSince ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/e6090f180976846ce7a2e6e8d696a0fa078a471c950de6188908528c881839fb.svg) the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/792ff38b4658d1d4bbfbc57cbe93be95dd8d90b24559f601250eaa81becf8d24.svg) we get\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/c5a00088d2fcc7951b02f0291e50136dd7e4bd2a53f188dfc498645eb26929aa.svg)",
